{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The American thesis of free-market capitalism \nis that privatization breeds competition,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "competition forces merit, merit compels \ninnovation, and innovation lowers prices. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the U.S., private firms are \nencouraged and allowed to dominate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire markets as winner take all.\nTheir monetary gains are the reward  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18880,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the public value they create, \nwhether that’s healthcare, utilities,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surveillance, telecoms, or even education.\nEverything is done under the theory that free,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minimally regulated markets \nproduce the greatest innovation. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But look around these days, and the \ncountry seems to be proving the opposite. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Privatization has reshaped and consolidated \nmarkets over decades into oligarchies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where access has shrunk to a handful of \nincreasingly expensive options designed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to benefit shareholders over consumers.\nHealthcare, housing, medicine, gas,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and groceries are daily essentials \nwhere everyone feels this squeeze. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one industry has raised prices just \nas fast and shrunk access even further and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the one nobody thinks to call a market at \nall: college - the one purchase every American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is told they need to succeed.\nNowhere in the world is college  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more expensive than in the United States.\nThe world-famous American universities — Harvard,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stanford, Princeton, MIT — \nall charge six figures a year. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75440,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Families invest years in advance \njust for a shot at getting in,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this has spawned an entire separate \nindustry of consultants, test-prep companies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essay editors, and extracurricular coaches.\nIf we take a closer, more critical look,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America's elite universities are \nreally more like luxury brands. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're privatized businesses built on carefully \nmanufactured scarcity, compounded over centuries. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like Hermès or Ferrari, these schools have \ndeliberately kept enrollment flat for decades even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as demand has exploded by orders of magnitude.\nThese schools design campuses the way luxury  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "houses build stores like living temples \nof prestige, history, and culture. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And like Rolex or AP, they \ndon't make money on walk-ins. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They allocate seats to a clientele built \nover generations of purchase history and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make exceptions for the wealthy and powerful.\nIf college is a ticket to the middle class, these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "elite schools sell tickets to the upper class.\nGetting in is marketed as lifelong  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proof of superiority and intelligence.\nBut as anyone who's worked in corporate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133040,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long enough knows, Harvard, MIT, Stanford, and \nIvy League grads are not objectively smarter. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From personal experience, they generally \nperform worse, spend more time talking than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doing , and are constantly reminding \neveryone where they went to college. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite their mythical status, these elite schools \nhave never produced data showing their teaching  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or job outcomes are any better. There is no \neducational justification for their selectivity. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their graduates walk out with the \nsame paper diplomas as everyone else. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Under this lens, America's elite colleges sell \nstatus, not education, and measure themselves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solely on how many applicants they turn away while \ntaking credit for the success of their alumni. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every graduating class completes the ritual \nand are given rings, jackets, ties, and other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176480,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "commemorative exclusives to carry into adulthood.\nThen with class reunions and alumni events  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in every city, the school never stops asking \ngraduates to donate money to the very institution  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186880,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that charged them six figures to attend.\nThere is something absurd about charging  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190960,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people nearly half a million dollars \nin cash for a piece of paper and then  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asking them to donate out of gratitude for \nthe four-year experience they paid for. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198880,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet it works - billions flow back to these \ninstitutions annually and these elite schools  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203920,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regularly rake in more donations in a single year \nthan most universities raise in a generation. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From this angle, Stanford, Harvard, MIT, \nPrinceton, Yale, UPenn, and Columbia are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more like cults, banks, and cartels that \nlive on a pyramid of contradictions. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219200,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're non-profits, yet sit on more cash than \nNike, Disney, McDonald's, Coca-Cola, and Boeing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They charge six figures, \ncollect millions in donations,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and hoard billions in reserves — yet remain \nfederally funded and pay little to no tax. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233840,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They appoint presidents no one ever \nmeets and pay them millions a year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a job no student can even describe.\nThey employ the most celebrated scientists  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and researchers alive — and give \nevery discovery away for free. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their biggest buildings are funded by donations.\nThey lose money on almost everything they do,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and still get richer every single year.\nUltimately, America’s elite colleges are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255040,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so complex that the best way to \nunderstand how they make money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is through strategy games like Starcraft, \nCivilization, Age of Empires and Total War. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In these video games, you win by assembling the \nmost powerful units, unlocking the most advanced  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tech trees, building the most productive economy, \nconstructing wonders that generate culture,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "planting seeds to harvest turns later, \nor spreading reputation like a religion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across the map - all while paying maintenance \non centuries of decisions and infrastructure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like what Harvard, Stanford, Yale, \nMIT, and Princeton do every single day. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this episode, we break down how America's most \nprestigious universities actually make money and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why every contradiction on the list makes sense \nonce you see the game they’re really playing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "RTS games boil down to 4 core mechanics: \nmacro, micro, tech, and production. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Macro is about building the most productive \neconomy possible with a steady stream of income,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maximizing worker efficiency, and constant \nexpansion to new resources as soon as they emerge. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312880,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America's elite universities run this \nsame playbook through 3 divisions. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316880,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first 2 are advancement and \nendowment, which work together on economy. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320800,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The third is administration, which spends \nthe economy and owns everything it buys:  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the supply cap, the tech tree, which units \nto recruit and which buildings to construct. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every RTS game begins with forests, mines, or \nfarms - and the college business is the same way. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Advancement produces the workers, farmers, \nand probes, except in this case, the only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "resource they care about is cash.\nSome schools call it advancement,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "others brand it development or alumni \naffairs - but it’s all the same thing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s a sales org dressed up as school spirit \nwhose only goal is to harvest as much new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money as it can into the school’s coffers.\nIf you’ve ever received a letter, cold call,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357040,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or email from your alma mater \nasking you to give back or donate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you’ve interfaced with this exact department.\nEvery graduate is a potential harvest and the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wealthier, more powerful, and more generous you \nget, the more closely this department watches you. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370720,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Under this lens, undergrads \nare not recruited units,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead seeds that scatter after graduation.\nWhile players harvest for immediate income in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strategy games, universities plant seeds \nwith the goal of harvesting decades later. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike gold veins or mineral patches that \nrun dry, students are a renewable resource. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388960,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every graduating class is a planting \nscattered out into the world and every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incoming class of freshman reseeds the field.\nAs long as the university provides a good  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397280,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "undergrad experience, it gives itself \na chance to harvest down the line. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the elite American universities are \nnot just the richest — they're the richest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're the oldest, with more \nharvests behind them than anyone else. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet while resources occur naturally in \nvideo games, in colleges, the seeds pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "six figures for the privilege of being planted.\nLike any good RTS player knows, the best econ  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requires maximum collection at minimal cost.\nAlumni reunions, networking dinners,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and annual giving drives are free parties that the \ncollege throws, not because it loves its students,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because it helps them make money.\nThese events let them track your career,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432560,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "record your financial status, and score your \nchances of donating, no different than what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a sales team does with prospects in Salesforce.\nWhenever you answer the call, attend the reunion,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or fill out the survey, you're \nhelping the college time its harvest. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Princeton operates the most effective advancement \ndepartment in the country and boasts the highest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450400,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rate of donor participation from living graduates.\nAlumni volunteers enthusiastically solicit their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456320,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own classmates and as unpaid laborers, the \ncost of collection to the school is near-zero. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every graduating class competes \nannually to see who donates the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most and elects an officer whose entire job \nis manufacturing the spirit to give back. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469760,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Harvard has its famous Red \nBook, which is a scrapbook that students  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473680,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diligently fill out every 5 years.\nIt’s really a prospect database  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where alumni self-report their careers, \nlocations, and salaries so the school  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never has to pay anyone to compile it.\nAnd at every one of these universities,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "someone is getting paid full-time to watch for \nany big liquidity events like an IPO, company  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sale, inheritance, or executive appointment, \nbecause those are the best moments to harvest. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But generosity alone isn’t enough.\nEvery college hires full-time salesmen, who are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500480,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called gift officers, and assigns them an annual \nquota and portfolio of high net worth alumni. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505760,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their job is to wine-and-dine each \nof these individuals into upping  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their donations to six and seven figures.\nBut at the elite universities, writing a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check for thousands or millions \nonly makes you a mid-tier donor. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516800,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real rewards are reserved for \nthe eight and nine-figure whales. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are the 1% of the 1%, who donate \nto either guarantee their kids admission  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524880,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or because they’re so rich that the \nonly thing left to buy is immortality. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These whales are so few, so lucrative, and so \nimportant that they get the personal attention of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every university’s president, deans, and trustees.\nThis is why no student ever really meets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or interacts with the college president.\nThey’ll give an occasional speech or pen a letter,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but all their time is dedicated to closing the \nwhales, rather than the unripe undergrads who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are decades away from writing a check.\nIn exchange, the children, relatives,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and close friends of the big \ndonors get guaranteed admission. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555120,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But undergrads are still critical.\nThe years between eighteen to twenty-two  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the most formative periods of a person's life. \nThis is when kids legally become adults, discover  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves, find friends, and choose careers.\nColleges insert themselves into this exact  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "window by design with the bet that all this \ngoodwill and nostalgia can be liquidated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574240,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decades later into millions in donations.\nIn contrast, graduate alumni and PhDs are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580080,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proven to donate substantially less.\nTheir relationship with the school  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is transactional and their attendance is \nlinked to a specific professional outcome. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the priority of every elite \ncollege is the same, which is to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make undergrad life as engaging, happy, and \ntight-knit for as little cost as possible. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any and every future donation hinges \non delivering that experience. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to manufacture a deep connection with \neach student, every class has to stay small. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, public universities \nlike the UCs suffer from the exact  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problem that the private elites avoid.\nWhen you enroll tens of thousands of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613200,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "students every year, it’s impossible \nto foster deep tribal bonds between  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "student to student or student to school.\nThus, the elite colleges intentionally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fragment their already small \nclasses into even smaller cohorts. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s like the Sorting Hat from Harry Potter, \nwhere getting into Hogwarts is one thing,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the house you end up in is really what shapes \nyour daily life, social circle, and identity. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yale sorts freshmen into 14 different residential \ncolleges, each with its own dining hall,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "library, and gym, and every undergrad stays \naffiliated with it for their entire 4 years. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644960,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Harvard has 12 houses, each with \ntheir own traditions, merchandise,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sporting teams and the assignment itself \nis a ritual, where upperclassmen storm into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freshman dorms dressed in costumes.\nPrinceton randomly assigns freshmen  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to residential colleges and then pushes \nupperclassmen into one of eleven eating clubs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which open up a deeper social world where members \neat together and party in their own mansions. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stanford and Columbia, in contrast, have \nnever managed to engineer the same level  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of physical tribalism as Greek life \nand co-ops have dominated for decades. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every university deliberately \nlayers on even more tribes like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "acapella groups, frats, sororities, and clubs.\nThe more memberships a student holds, the more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their identity gets fused with the school itself.\nThe same logic applies to housing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The elite universities house a far larger \nnumber of their undergrads for far longer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than any other public or private university.\nOver 9 out of every 10 Harvard and Princeton  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "undergrads live on campus for all four years.\nThe schools eat this cost not out of generosity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703520,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but instead as part of an investment \nin connection and future donations. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707440,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also field an absurdly high \nratio of athletic offerings with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one varsity team for every 150 students.\nAt public universities, men’s football and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716640,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basketball are commercial products whose revenues \nsubsidize the other two dozen sports offered. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The elite colleges opt out \nof this business entirely. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No Ivy League school competes at the top \nof football or basketball and athletic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scholarships have been banned for over 70 years.\nThus, their sprawling athletic departments all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "run at a loss, are uncompetitive, and exist \nonly for school spirit and student bonding. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The few sports they dominate like squash, crew, \nsailing, and fencing are just a reflection of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the preppy, upper-class families that \nmost of their student bodies come from. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only Stanford competes at the \ntop in football and basketball,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even its program has needed rescuing.\nLike housing, athletics are aggressively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidized so that students can have another \nlayer of attachment to the institution. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In RTS terms, the dorms, dining halls, gyms, \nand stadiums are all happiness buildings. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’re capital investments to keep the population \nsatisfied with the aim of cultivating memories and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "converting them into donations decades later.\nOnly the elites can afford to play this game  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776480,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as they get to concentrate all their \ninvestment in a small student body. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet the twist is that the most reliable donors \nare not the whales, but instead the students who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785120,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could never have afforded to attend.\nThe first-generation, low-income,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scholarship kids who attend on someone else’s \nmoney, make it big, and want to pay it forward  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the most consistent donors - and their faces \nand stories of “this school changed my life” are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the centerpiece of every school’s marketing.\nEvery campus is full of trust fund kids who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were born rich, coast through the 4 years, and \nnever donate and the universities know that. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the best colleges carefully engineer \nthe composition of every incoming class by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "choosing the right seeds, even if that means \npaying for the planting themselves when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "necessary with financial aid and balancing these \nsubsidized cohorts with the rest who pay in full. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821040,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every college runs this formula, \nbut the elite universities hold  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the single greatest advantage in time.\nIf you were given 20 to 40 turns to build  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up your econ before your competition \nspawns, you too would be unstoppable. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While advancement brings in new money, endowment \ngrows the old money that’s already banked. In an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "RTS, you never want to hoard resources.\nBut colleges are the opposite. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841680,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They want to hoard capital, because every \nbuilding and professor brings on decades  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of liabilities and overhead, so they must be \ndiligent about what they build and who they hire. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second reason is that \nthere’s no true win condition. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you’re Harvard or MIT, you’re already at \nthe top and there’s nowhere left to go but down. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And unlike any conventional business where \nmarket share requires expansion, Harvard and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MIT have to stay small, scarce, and physically \nrooted in Cambridge to preserve their brands. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The endowment division’s only job is to \nmake the pile of money bigger every year. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why endowment managers are the \nhighest-paid staff at every university,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "often recruited from Wall Street \nand rake in millions more than the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "presidents and provosts that they serve.\nTheir investments are measured in decades,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their mandate is to maximize returns \nevery year so the school can fund as much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888400,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the student experience from passive \nincome for today and future generations. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why the elite colleges invest so much \nof their endowment in private equity and venture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capital, rather than T-bills and index funds.\nThey’re chasing alpha and those unicorn returns,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902960,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if realized, can carry the \nschool for the next 50 years. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also why any framing of America’s top \nuniversities like Harvard, Columbia, Yale,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "etc. as bastions of social \nresponsibility, free speech,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and independent thought is false and \ncollapses with the school’s business model. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The returns that fund the school come \nfrom the same vilified industries that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their student bodies and faculty protest.\nEvery year, the school draws down roughly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "five percent of the endowment's value to \nspend while everything else remains invested. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This payout happens on time regardless \nof whether the markets go up or down. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That way, the endowment smooths over any \nbad years and the school always gets funded. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941440,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when the losses occur, hiring freezes are \nput in-place, PhD cohorts get cut down, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "non-tenured professors are asked to leave.\nYet the greatest irony is that despite being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the longest bull market in history, these \nuniversities have all failed to beat the market,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even with their million-dollar Wall \nStreet managers and connections. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957920,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After fees and on net returns, nearly \nevery school has underperformed a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "run-of-the-mill Vanguard index fund and \nno one has lost out on more than Harvard. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But getting above market returns is so critical \nbecause the elite colleges financially handicap  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves on the primary revenue source \nfor every other university in the world. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975440,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With artificially capped enrollment, undergrad \ntuition is a loss leader where most seats get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "subsidized through financial aid to attract \nand cultivate that future eight-figure donor. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985680,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, endowment covers two thirds of the \nannual operating budget at these universities,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990720,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with Princeton being the most extreme.\nYet it’s a different story for the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "graduate and professional programs, where \nthese schools admit far more students,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "charge higher tuition, and hand out far less aid.\nAt Columbia, undergrads contribute less  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than one fifth of net tuition.\nBut everyone knows that getting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into Harvard grad school is not the \nsame as getting into Harvard college. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why grad students outnumber undergrads by \nmultiples at every elite university, because they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intentionally freeze the undergrad brand but \nscale everything else around it to make money. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The final nuance is that endowment \nis not just one pot of money. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s thousands of individually restricted \nfunds where most of the money is legally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bound to whatever purpose its donor specified.\nIf a donor says their money can only be used  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fund the library, the school can't legally \nuse it to patch a hole in any other building,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038080,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even as a temporary bridge loan.\nDonor restrictions are binding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "contracts that are enforceable for centuries \nby the donor’s heirs and state attorneys. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why the small-dollar annual \ngiving drives are still invaluable. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though most alumni only give \ntwo, three, or four figures at most,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these donations are unrestricted.\nIt’s money that the college can spend anywhere  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it wants whereas the eight and nine-figure gifts \nfrom the whales always come with strings attached. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This brings us to the third and most \nconsequential division - administration. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’re the department that spends \nthe budget, recruits the faculty,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shapes student life, chooses which facilities \nto build versus renovate, and decides what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "branches of the tech tree to invest in.\nThis division is where the school’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prestige is manufactured and maintained.\nThe real power here lies with the provost. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The provost sets the budget for every \ndepartment, decides who gets hired,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dictates what parts of the tech tree get \nresearched, and takes reports from every dean. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Provosts are the ones who actually run the \nuniversity, and they hold power over which fields  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and faculty thrive or starve at the institution.\nThe most powerful unit a college can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102080,
    "dDurationMs": 1483,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recruit is its faculty.\nBut money is the constraint  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103563,
    "dDurationMs": 1957,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and every provost rations headcount.\nEvery hire runs through the provost and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they must judge whether that extra payroll will \nserve the school best here or would be better  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off allocated to a different department.\nUnlike the private sector where you can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hire anyone with money alone, \nuniversities run on slots. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every department holds a fixed number \nof authorized faculty positions. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After 6 years of service, every hired \nprofessor comes up for tenure review. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If approved, that once-flexible hire becomes \na permanent obligation, where the university  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129680,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "commits to paying their salary and benefits for \nthe next 40 plus years with no termination date. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Colleges cannot legally fire or force \nout tenured professors to reclaim budget. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also why the tenured faculty are insulated \nduring budget cuts and the pain lands entirely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the at-will lecturers, assistants, \npostdocs, and manual workers below them. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, once a professor gets \ntenure, they generally never leave. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A slot only reopens once a tenured professor \nretires, dies, or leaves the university entirely. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159440,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The provost then gets to choose \nif that headcount should stay or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162400,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be moved to a different department.\nRe-allocating slots from shrinking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "departments to growing ones is arguably the \nmost important decision a provost can make. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A losing department reads the headcount \nloss as an indictment of its future. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1174560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its non-tenured faculty interpret it as a sign \nto jump ship — and as the talent bleeds out,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179440,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the students left behind get a worse \neducation from a shrinking department "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, the winning departments thrive.\nGetting new slots is proof that the school  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "believes in the future of their field \nand is willing to invest in them. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In RTS terms, this is like \nsupply depots or pylons. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can sit on all the cash in the \nworld and still be supply blocked. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As rich as they are, the elites can’t just \ncasually dish out headcount because a single  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tenured professor is a lifetime commitment \nthat can total tens of millions of dollars. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206640,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s no way to undo or delete \nthis labor cost once committed. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210080,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the biggest issue of all is that \nno one can know whether a field will  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1213360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still matter in 30 years.\nEvery field is like a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stock which goes up and down.\nThe flood of venture capital,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the young billionaire founders, and the \nsix-figure new grad salaries have propelled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "computer science from a niche degree into \nthe most popular major in the past decade. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unsurprisingly, provosts everywhere \nhave plowed headcount into their CS  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232080,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "departments to meet demand.\nOver the same period,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "humanities enrollment has evaporated and every \ntenured professor in English or Literature  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is one less headcount for the CS department.\nNuclear engineering is another great example. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1245520,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1970s, it was the future and American \nuniversities poured millions into labs, reactors,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tenured faculty to feed what seemed to \nbe the energy source of the next century. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chernobyl single-handedly killed any appetite \nfor the field and those same schools spent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the next 40 years paying salaries for a \ndepartment that nobody wanted to major in. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, it’s far more dangerous to permanently \noverbuild for a shrinking field than it is to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temporarily underinvest in a growing one.\nUltimately, refusing to grow supply is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part of the DNA for the elite schools.\nThe same selectivity applied to students  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is also applied to faculty and there’s \nlittle merit in doubling a department’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "headcount when the student body is capped.\nIn summary, every department is a field,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1288640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every field represents a branch of \nthe tech tree, and investing in that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "department means investing in that branch.\nAs a result, the provost isn’t just allocating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296960,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hires as much as they are choosing which \nbranches to research, which to divest,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and which to maintain, to strengthen \nthe school’s prestige and leadership. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In an RTS, every investment in the tech tree is \npermanent and comes with guaranteed upgrades. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310480,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But real life is the opposite.\nYou can’t buy an outcome. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All you can do is buy the people \nthat might achieve a breakthrough,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is exactly what colleges do.\nAnd when you finish research in an RTS,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that tech remains permanent and free forever.\nIn contrast, a university department  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1326080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remains permanent and expensive forever.\nThus, getting the tech tree right is a matter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330560,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of upkeep as much as selection, where everything \nyou build and everyone you hire costs money every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn, whether or not it’s producing.\nAt the same time, the tech  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tree in real life is dynamic.\nIf we say every field is a branch,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345760,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then branches sprout, fuse together into new \nlimbs, split, or simply wither away over time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bioengineering didn’t exist in the 80s and \nyet the field today boasts departments,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356000,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "PhD programs, and journals worldwide.\nCognitive science fused out of psychology,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358833,
    "dDurationMs": 3007,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "linguistics, philosophy, and computer science.\nThese days, quantum, climate, and AI are new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "branches that are all blossoming on the tech tree.\nLike in an RTS, a college can always tech-rush  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and aggressively plow resources into \na specific branch it’s bullish on. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371120,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But hiring doesn't solve execution.\nIf the researchers it hires don't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outperform their peers at other schools, then \nthe school has blown its economy and headcount. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the tech tree is so big and all the \nedge comes from depth rather than breadth,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500880,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every university must specialize to succeed. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But no individual can achieve \ncutting-edge research on their own. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A world-class researcher needs surrounding \nfaculty as co-authors, grad students to push  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the work forward day-to-day, and enough scale \nto justify the additional millions of dollars  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1516240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in special equipment that their work demands.\nThus, universities can’t just throw money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to hire the biggest stars in the \ntrendiest fields and call it a day. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No matter how good they are, their execution \nwill be slow, unproductive, and risky without  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529120,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the support directly around them.\nUnder this lens, only with a critical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass of resources, talent, and infrastructure \ncan a college assemble an acclaimed top-five  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "department that publishes the field’s \nbest papers, attracts the strongest PhDs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1542320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and owns state-of-the-art facilities that \ndonors are willing to pay to put their name on. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if a university stays stingy or spreads its \ninvestment too thin, then every department just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exists to teach and produces no cutting-edge \nresearch, no talent, and no prestige. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, professors are \nwhat make every university. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remove the famous faculty and star researchers \nand all the overachieving undergrads and PhDs have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1565280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little reason to attend beyond the brand itself.\nBy this logic, the elite universities are forever  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assembling armies of the best professors \nas hero units concentrated in the branches  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1574880,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they believe to be the most critical.\nMeanwhile, the lower-ranked colleges below  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them have to pay up big to poach whoever they can \nin an attempt to buy their way onto the tech tree. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the main conundrum is that \neven if the research is successful,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the school captures none of its economic value.\nBreakthrough research is generally not patented  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or licensed, but instead given away.\nProfessors move up their fields based on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1595760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publications, citations, and peer review - all \nof which requires their work to be publicized. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1601200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any university that locks up research \nfor monetization would immediately  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1604960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "destroy the prestige that attracts faculty, \nstudents, and applicants in the first place. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1609760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the elite schools, the vast majority of \nundergrads never even see the Nobel-winning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1614160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faculty on campus — yet they're still elevated \nby their association, proximity, and reputation. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ve explained the how and what, but the \nquestion still remains - why do schools bother  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1624400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investing in research if they lose money on it?\nNo matter what branch you choose, it’s all a money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pit - yet the stakes are bigger than they look.\nNearly every major industry today started  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as an experiment in a campus lab \nyears ahead of the private sector. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Corporate America abandoned long-horizon \nresearch decades ago as shareholders demand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "returns every quarter and results \ntake generations to materialize. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America’s universities are the only remaining \ninstitutions in the country that can make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1650160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these bets and are willing to wait 20 \nyears or more for a non-monetary payoff. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1654880,
    "dDurationMs": 3379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The mRNA technology behind the COVID \nvaccines was discovered at UPenn. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1658259,
    "dDurationMs": 1181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Recombinant DNA - which birthed the \nmodern biotech industry, PageRank - which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "organized the public web and became Google, and \noptogenetics - the defining tool of present-day  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1664720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "neuroscience -all came out of Stanford.\nAnd the open-source cryptography that encrypts  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1669280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything you do online from the messages you \nsend to the things you buy was invented at MIT. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just a partial list of all the \ncutting-edge technologies birthed by America’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1678560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "elite universities - and all of this is by design.\nThe federal government uses taxpayer money to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reimburse schools for the costs of research, \nbecause they know that this work would never  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1688080,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get funded if left to the private sector.\nEven if a for-profit company did  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1692400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "achieve a breakthrough, it would \npredictably hoard the knowledge  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1695040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of releasing it for the public good.\nUnder this lens, the whole system is engineered  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1699920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around a simple division of labor, where the \nuniversities drive research, incubate talent, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publish the knowledge for free while the private \nsector builds products around their discoveries. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a company likes what it sees, it can \nsimply poach the PhD or professor to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1714720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "private sector with a life-changing salary \nwithout having to go through the university. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1719200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the next time someone proclaims the U.S. as \nthe land of free-market capitalism, just point  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1724000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them to the university system, where innovation \nis federally subsidized and then commercialized by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1729120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corporations who sell to taxpayers at a markup.\nNearly every great American technology traces  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back to federally-funded university research.\nThe U.S. government built it this way on purpose,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1739440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because keeping America in the driver’s \nseat of innovation and talent is a far  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1743280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more important geopolitical priority than \ncomplete worship of free market ideology. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But getting federal funding \nis extremely competitive. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s fifty schools chasing after the same \ngrants and only the winners get to keep going. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These grants reimburse universities \nnot just for the cost of payroll,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1759120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but also infrastructure like construction, \nutilities, security, and maintanence. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even the tenured salaries, the one cost that a \nschool can never escape, get partially reimbursed. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, the \ngovernment has its own agenda. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1772160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They run the same VC playbook that we \ncovered in our video on Chinese EVs where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1776880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they intentionally pour the most funding into \nthe fields that they deem critical, in order  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1781120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to steer research towards federal priorities.\nThus, whenever a provost is trying to figure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786320,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out which branch of the tech tree to invest \nin, they’re evaluating reimbursement potential  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1790560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as much as talent and infrastructure.\nIn short, the tech tree is shaped less  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1794880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by science and more by national priorities.\nWhen Congress doubled the National Institutes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Health budget in the late 90s, the cost \nof biomedical research was cut in half,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1804000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the elite colleges responded by pouring \nmillions into new buildings and star faculty. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1808960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This dependence on Uncle Sam is why \nthe narrative of America’s elite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1812560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universities as some mythical sanctuary of \nindependent thought really makes no sense. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1817280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any cut to federal funding destroys their entire \nbusiness model and no school is dumb enough to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bite the hand that feeds - especially if it's done \njust to appease subsidized undergrads - the people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1827120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the lowest Net Present Value on campus.\nThis is why humanities is underinvested everywhere  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the field gets near-zero federal funding.\nWorld-renowned humanities departments like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1837600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yale English, Harvard Classics, and Princeton \nphilosophy earned their reputations generations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1843040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ago, under entirely different economics.\nNow they're simply maintained as inherited  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1847920,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infrastructure, talent, and \nassets that no university  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1850960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could afford to build from scratch today.\nSo to recap, colleges recruit professors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they chase the superstar faculty and renowned \nresearchers in the fields they want to invest in. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1860880,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These stars are like hero units that bring talent, \nnetworks, grants, and government relationships  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1866000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with them, all of which turns research from \na money pit into a federally-subsidized  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1870400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "activity that elevates the school’s profile.\nBut academics are generally not mercenaries. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're not strictly motivated by money in \nthe same way like it is in the private sector. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1879760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Researchers at the top of their field \nrequire state-of-the-art buildings  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1882960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and equipment that can enable them to \nadvance their research to new heights. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These facilities are one of a kind with custom \nbuilt features like electro-polished pipe,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1891440,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hazardous gas ventilation, specialized \ncleanrooms, and vibration-isolated foundations. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1896960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of this infrastructure must exist \nbefore a single federal dollar shows up. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1901280,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reimbursement is never given \nin advance and only applies to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1904560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "research performed in completed buildings.\nA big donor typically only covers a third  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1909120,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the cost in exchange for slapping their \nname on the building while the rest must  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1912880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come out of the school’s pocket.\nIt’s a chicken-and-egg problem. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1916160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A university can front construction with endowment \nmoney in the hopes of winning over star faculty,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1921120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the building can become an overbuilt \nliability if that talent never comes. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1925440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alternatively, it can recruit the stars first \nand then build later but then those same hero  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1930000,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "units it fought so hard to win will get \npoached right back if the infrastructure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "takes too long to materialize.\nEither way, every new building,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1937520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like every key hire, permanently adds \noverhead that only the endowment can carry. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1942480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet with 90 to 95 percent of the annual \nbudget already committed to tenured salaries,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1947520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "financial aid, debt service, and maintenance \non everything already standing, universities  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1952800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only have 5 to 10% leftover to spend.\nAs a result, they naturally pursue new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1957680,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "construction because donors will pay eight and \nnine figures to slap their name on the latest,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1961920,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shiniest building but never \nfor repairs on an old one. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1965120,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the result is the same at all schools, \nwhere renovations are continually deferred  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1969520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and new construction matches whatever branch \nof the tech tree the university is chasing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1974080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even when everything goes right \nin construction and recruitment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1977200,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the research can still fail.\nThe star hire never wins funding, gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1981120,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tenure anyways, and becomes a permanent liability.\nThe field cools in the middle of construction. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1986560,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The federal agency cuts off the \ngrants to pursue a new direction. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1990160,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In every one of these scenarios, the school \nends up with buildings and units that drain  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1994720,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money forever. And since academia is a \nsmall world, every failure compounds. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1995600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a university makes promises it doesn’t deliver, \nword travels fast and every broken one stains  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2001120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its ability to recruit in the future.\nAll this makes research a dangerous  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2005040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game for any school trying to climb the ranks.\nIf you nail it, your prestige grows exponentially,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2010080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you’re wrong, you bleed for decades.\nIf you put yourself in the shoes of an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2013920,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up-and-coming researcher or scientist, there's \nno reason to ever consider the lesser schools. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2018640,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They'll give you more money, but the \npaycheck is the only thing they can offer. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2022240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you take it, you'd effectively \nbe sidelining your own career. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every year at a lesser school is \nanother year wasted, and by the end,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2028800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'll have lost decades idling when you could \notherwise have been doing your best work. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2032960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, the rational move for academics \nis to prove themselves wherever they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2036880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are and then jump to the elites.\nThere is no upside to purposely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2040560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distancing yourself from the hubs of \nleading talent, funding, relationships,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2044640,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and infrastructure that already exist.\nAnd more likely than not, the Nobel laureate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2049120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they have down the hall or talented postdoc next \ndoor will be the missing inspiration, guidance,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2054400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or collaborator you didn’t know you needed.\nPrinceton has taken a piecemeal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2058480,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "approach over the decades.\nThrough the 2000s, their researchers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2061680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "patiently worked out of borrowed, second-rate \nlab space while the school compiled donations. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2066240,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They collected $20M from alumnus Carl \nIcahn to build a new state-of-the-art  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2070960,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lab and $50M from the alumni and founder of \nProgressive Insurance for a science library. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2076880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The university poached stars like David Botstein \nfrom Stanford to lead its new genomics institute,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2082320,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and David in turn recruited the world-renowned \nfaculty that now lead the school’s DNA research. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2088240,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, in-house talent like \nBonnie Bassler who had been with Princeton  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2092160,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since the 90s would grow to become the \nworld’s leading molecular biologist. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2096240,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While every other school invested in life \nsciences to chase the newly doubled NIH budget,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2101360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Princeton opted for a different approach.\nThe university wired the biomedical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2105280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "branch into its existing, acclaimed \ndepartments of math, physics, chemistry,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and CS — to tackle life science research as \na data problem rather than a clinical one. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2113680,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 2010s, Princeton completed four \nmore hero buildings, led by a $100M energy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2119360,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "center and a $180M neuroscience institute with \nfour-ton MRIs — both funded entirely by donors. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2126800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Emily Carter, a world-renowned computational \nchemist, was recruited to turn the new  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2131600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy center into a flourishing asset.\nShe hired the faculty, designed the programs, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2136640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "oversaw the construction — and did so well that \nshe was later promoted to dean of engineering. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2141520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jennifer Rexford chaired the computer science \ndepartment as CS exploded into Princeton's most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2146560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "popular major, and did so well that she was later \npromoted to provost of the entire university. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2151920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From this angle, the hero units \naren't just lab scientists. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2155360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They can also be operators who can \nidentify talent, scale departments,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2159120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and organize programs that convert donor \nmoney and empty buildings into outcomes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2163440,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that grow a school’s profile and productivity.\nUltimately, Princeton has followed the same  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2167360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pattern over the past 25 years.\nThey enter new fields through  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2171120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantitative theory to avoid having \nto build expensive, labor-intensive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2175040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clinical infrastructure like hospitals.\nNew buildings get funded again and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2179120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again by the same billionaire alumni.\nWith no medical school, no law school,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2183280,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and no business school, Princeton \nhas stayed ruthlessly narrow. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2186560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The university is exclusively dependent on its \nendowment and even though they spend a fifth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2190880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of what Harvard does on research, they remain on \npar or superior in every field they play in - all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2196320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while making sure that their star faculty have \nlittle reason to take their talents anywhere else. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2201040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MIT has taken the opposite approach.\nThe university has so much wealth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2204960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it can fund capital projects upfront.\nIn the 2000s, MIT built the world’s largest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2210400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "neuroscience center, which was funded \nby a $350M pledge from the alumnus and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2215520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "founder of PC World and Computerworld.\nMeanwhile, billionaire philanthropists  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2220400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eli and Edith Broad plowed $700M \ninto a new biomedical institute. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2225840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of poaching talent from outside its walls, \nMIT simply staffed these new buildings with the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2230880,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nobel laureates it already had on payroll.\nAnd without a hospital of its own,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2235360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the school partnered with Harvard to gain \naccess to the patients and clinical trials  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2239840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "necessary for biomedical research.\nIt was in the 20 10s when MIT  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2244160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started making bets with its own money.\nThe university sank $400M into building one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2249520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the nation’s largest nanofabrication \nfacilities with no donor at all. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2253920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The infrastructure was deemed too critical \nto wait and so MIT built first and sold the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2258160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "naming rights later, four years after \nopening, to alumna and AMD’s Lisa Su. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2263040,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Blackstone’s CEO donated $350M to charter a new \ncollege of computing, which consolidated double-E,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2270240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "CS, and AI departments under one roof and \nadded 50 new slots for tenured faculty. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2275760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, its hero units delivered \nbreakthroughs with the first technology  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2279280,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for human genome editing, expansion microscopy, \nand the first ever antibiotic made by AI. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2285360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2025, MIT had spun off its federally-funded \nfusion research into a for-profit startup,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2291600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which has since built a record-breaking \n20-tesla magnet to enable the world’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2295520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first, net positive fusion reactor. MIT’s \nstrategy is all about tools over trophies. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2301200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its researchers focus on developing \nplatform technologies or instruments  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2304960,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can be given away for free, so entire \nindustries will standardize on MIT’s work. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2310320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Computing is the universal entry point, aimed \nat the adjacent branches of biomedicine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2314880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pharmaceutical, and energy.\nAlumni front the buildings, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2318400,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "school spends next to nothing on amenities, and \nits research naturally flows towards products and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2323280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "startups - all of which leaves MIT less dependent \non federal funding than nearly everyone else. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2329040,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Harvard, in contrast, has struggled.\nWhile every other elite university is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2333280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "centralized, Harvard is really twelve \nseparate schools that share one brand. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2337360,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each school runs its own budget and \nendowment and the president controls  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2340800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost none of it as most donations are legally \nrestricted to the school that raised them. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2345840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through the 2000s, Larry Summers tried \nto fix this fragmentation as Harvard’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2350000,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "president by building a $1.4B flagship complex \nacross the river that would double Harvard's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2355760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physical footprint and pull all the scattered \nsciences into one interdisciplinary campus. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2361120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when the endowment crashed 30% in the Great \nRecession, there was no pooled reserve to rescue  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2366240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the project even though the individual \nschools were each sitting on billions. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2370480,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "None of those funds could be legally \nredirected or lent to the administration. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2374480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Caught mid-construction, the university had no \nchoice but to pause the work and the abandoned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2379040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foundation sat there for the next 6 years.\nBecause of this fragmentation, Harvard’s tech  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2383760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tree is not determined by a central provost.\nInstead, branches are directly initiated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2388160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the wealthy alumni of each school.\nSteve Ballmer donated $60M to Harvard  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2393280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fund 12 new CS faculty slots in the hopes \nof elevating the engineering school to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2398320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same pedigree as MIT and Stanford.\nHedge-fund billionaire John Paulson  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2402640,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gifted another $400M with the same aim.\nMeanwhile, a Hong Kong billionaire paid $350M  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2409120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to slap his name on the School of Public Health.\nIt was and remains Harvard's poorest school.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2414160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Public health grads earn \nlittle and donate even less. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2417280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With a tiny endowment, the \nuniversity was glad to sell. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2420400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Harvard's leaders aren't dumb enough to sell \nthe naming rights for its most famous schools  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2424880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like College, Business, Law, and Medicine.\nUltimately, where Harvard dominates is in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2430320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "medicine, thanks to the network \nof affiliated hospitals that it’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2433680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accumulated for over more than a century.\nThe school boasts the largest concentration  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2438080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of research-hospital capacity in the world \nand provides researchers with unmatched  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2442560,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "access to patients and trials.\nBut without a unified command,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2446240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strategy is not coordinated and everything \nmoves slowly - 13 years for a single  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2451120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building and a growth in CS faculty that only \noccurred because a donor volunteered to pay. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2456480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Stanford thrives by using its \nresearch and campus to mint the next set  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2460720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of tech billionaires, who in turn fund \nthe next generation of the university. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2464880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 2000s, James Clark, a former professor \nand the founder of Silicon Graphics and Netscape,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2470080,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pledged $150M to build a facility for engineers, \ncomputer scientists, and medical researchers. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2476800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just two years after opening, Karl Deisseroth, \nwho was working inside the new Clark Center,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2481520,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uncovered the ability to switch \nbrain circuits on and off with light. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2485120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His discovery of optogenetics has become \nthe defining tool of modern neuroscience,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2489440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "used today in thousands of labs \nworldwide to map how the brain works. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2493440,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While MIT poached his collaborators, Stanford kept \nKarl, who would remain for the next two decades. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2499520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With its direct ties to Silicon Valley \nroyalty, the university has never needed money. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2504640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When your alumni mint billions at every IPO, \nyou don't need deadlines to compel donations. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2510160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, Stanford's tech tree is a \nsimple loop: research becomes companies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2514480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies become fortunes, fortunes become \ngifts, and gifts fund more research. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2519680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the next harvest is already \nripening with alumni like Jensen Huang,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2523520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Andrej Karpathy, and Sam Altman.\nYet all this groundbreaking research  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2527520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and infrastructure just maintains the brand.\nThe defining property of Harvard, Stanford,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2532080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Princeton is that their reputation \nis not attributed to any one field. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2535920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The brand by design sits above every department.\nTheir centuries of wealth, talent,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2540400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and infrastructure accumulation \nallow them to run wide tech trees. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2544240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whenever a new branch emerges, their brand \nbuys them instant credibility where the stars,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2548800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "donors, and applicants show up on Day 1 while \na lesser school would have to spend decades  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2553680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to earn that same trust and talent.\nThis is why single-branch dominance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2557200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the only play for the lower-ranked \nschools that are trying to climb up. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2560960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s the most capital-efficient path to prestige, \nwhere you can concentrate all your cash,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2565280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recruitment, infrastructure, and alumni \nwealth behind one single, specific field. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2570080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Babson throws everything into entrepreneurship.\nJohn Hopkins runs its entire brand on hospital,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2575280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "medicine, and public health.\nCarnegie Mellon is renowned for CS and robotics. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2579760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Georgetown law and government \nlifts everything else on campus. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2583280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Duke leads with medicine and basketball.\nPurdue and Georgia Tech specialize in engineering  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2588160,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while NYU is defined by Stern and Tisch.\nEvery one of these schools intentionally dominates  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2593760,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one or two branches and allows its mass-market \nreputation to ride entirely on those investments. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2599920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If faculty are the supply, \nthen students are the demand. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2603360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nobody turns down Stanford just because San \nJose State serves better food and provides a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2607680,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nicer mattress.\nStill,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2609200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the economics of happiness favor the elites.\nThe costs of amenities scale with population. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2614400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A school with capped enrollment can play tall \nand afford non-essential culture buildings  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2618720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like public art museums and libraries whereas a \nriser must play wide to unlock tuition revenue,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2624080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which linearly drives up housing, \ndining, health, and admin costs. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2628080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "None of it generates prestige and all of it \nmust be built before students even arrive. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2632480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In summary, undergrad scarcity is the \ncentral ingredient that fuels the brand. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2636720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The aura of Harvard, MIT, Stanford, and Princeton \nexists because most people can't get in. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2642400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What admissions officers optimize for is \nyield, which is the measure of whether  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2646400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your school is a first choice or a safety.\nOver the decades, the elite schools have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2650960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continually engineered higher yield rates as \na never-ending pissing match to be number one. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2655920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Early decision forces students into binding \nenrollment so they never get to compare offers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2660560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which in turn artificially boosts yield.\nUltimately, the admissions department exists  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2665280,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only to maintain prestige.\nMost admissions officers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2668000,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at these elite schools are not alumni.\nThey never attended the school themselves,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2671760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yet are paid to gate-keep and \npass judgement on who belongs. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2674960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're only there to preserve selectivity, \njust like the salespeople at Rolex and Hermes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2679200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stores who sit around guarding \ncases with nothing in them."
    } ]
  } ]
}
